# Code-page atoms demo (authored in ASCII \mnemonic form).
# Each line computes a single digit and prints it; output is "957444".
3\sqr 48+)            # 3 squared      = 9
4\inc 48+)            # 4 + 1          = 5
8\dec 48+)            # 8 - 1          = 7
2\dbl 48+)            # 2 * 2          = 4
9\hlv 48+)            # 9 >> 1         = 4
5\neg\inc\neg 48+)    # -(-5 + 1)      = 4
10)                   # newline
